# TextFSM template: Arista EOS `traceroute`.
#
# EOS shells out to the Linux userland `traceroute`, so the output
# is iputils-shaped. The FRR template for `traceroute` would also
# match this file — we keep them separate so vendor-specific
# decorations (probe markers, MTU annotations) can diverge later.
#
# Sample output:
#   traceroute to 1.1.1.1 (1.1.1.1) from 10.0.0.1, 30 hops max, 60 byte packets
#    1  gw.example.com (10.0.0.254)  0.234 ms
#    2  *
#    3  one.one.one.one (1.1.1.1)  10.123 ms
Value Filldown target (\S+)
Value Filldown source (\S+)
Value Required ttl (\d+)
Value ip ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value hostname ([\w.\-]+)
Value rtt_ms (\d+(?:\.\d+)?)

Start
  ^traceroute\s+to\s+\S+\s+\(${target}\)(?:\s+from\s+${source})?
  ^\s*${ttl}\s+${hostname}\s+\(${ip}\)\s+${rtt_ms}\s+ms -> Record
  ^\s*${ttl}\s+${ip}\s+${rtt_ms}\s+ms -> Record
  ^\s*${ttl}\s+\* -> Record
